  "## Strategy gene gene_unicode_nfkc_casefold\nDomain keywords: unicode, text-equality, nfc-lower-fails\nSummary: After NFC+lower and NFD+casefold both fail independently, upgrade to NFKC (compatibility) normalization with casefold() for complete Unicode equivalence.\nStrategy:\n1. Replace 'NFC' with 'NFKC' in normalize() call\u2014NFKC handles compatibility decompositions (ligatures, variant forms, precomposed characters)\n2. Replace .lower() with .casefold()\u2014proper Unicode case-folding for edge cases (\u00df\u2192ss, \u0131\u2192i, etc.)\n3. Apply as: normalize('NFKC', text).casefold()\n4. Test with ligatures (\ufb01), combining marks, diacritics (\u00e9), and special case pairs\n5. If NFKC+casefold fails, try reverse order: text.casefold() then normalize('NFKC', ...)\nAVOID:\n- Staying with NFC when compatibility equivalences matter (ligatures, vertical forms, character variants)\n- Using .lower() alone without .casefold() for Unicode text\u2014casefold handles edge cases .lower() misses\n- Switching normalization forms without reconsidering case-folding strategy; both must evolve together\n"
